{"author":{"id":"2462ded6f56967dde059994c39a506c79e39e5dfd10c5a07f07a23a5652a8353"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1775219291,"nonce":"sfcwbBrSI/2o77U1ZFUwY8vtQ6Y=","title":"Track token usage and cost per session permanently, surviving session cleanup.","message":"No token usage tracking exists. Claude Code emits `result` events with `cost_usd`, `input_tokens`, `output_tokens` but we ignore them. Session dirs are deleted on accept/reject/cleanup, so any per-session data is lost.\n\n\nTwo storage layers:\n\nAppend one JSON line to `.nightshift/usage.jsonl` when a session completes (before cleanup). Each line:\n```json\n{\"session_id\": \"abc123\", \"issue_id\": \"...\", \"title\": \"...\", \"agent_kind\": \"claude-code\", \"model\": \"claude-sonnet-4-6\", \"input_tokens\": 45000, \"output_tokens\": 12000, \"cost_usd\": 0.38, \"started_at\": \"...\", \"completed_at\": \"...\", \"resumes\": 3, \"step\": \"coder\"}\n```\n- File lives at `.nightshift/usage.jsonl` (outside session dirs, survives cleanup)\n- Gitignored (operational data)\n- Queryable: `nightshift usage` CLI command for filtering/aggregation\n\nAdd a one-line cost summary to the proof-of-work comment posted on session completion:\n```\n**Cost:** 45K input / 12K output tokens, $0.38 (claude-sonnet-4-6, 3 resumes)\n```\n\n- tests/test_session_runner.py::test_usage_accumulated_across_resumes\n  Assert: after 2 agent runs, state.usage.input_tokens is the sum of both\n- tests/test_session_runner.py::test_usage_from_result_event\n  Assert: when agent emits result event with cost_usd, state.usage is updated\n- tests/test_post_run.py::test_usage_appended_to_jsonl_on_done\n  Assert: after notify_done(), `.nightshift/usage.jsonl` has one new line with correct fields\n- tests/test_post_run.py::test_usage_jsonl_survives_cleanup\n  Assert: after cleanup, usage.jsonl still contains the entry\n- tests/test_launch.py::test_post_container_includes_cost_in_comment\n  Assert: proof-of-work comment contains \"Cost:\" line\n- tests/test_stream_parser.py::test_result_event_extracts_usage\n  Assert: ClaudeCodeAgent._parse() returns AgentEvent with usage metadata on result event\n\n- core/protocols.py (modify — add usage fields to AgentEvent or new UsageData dataclass)\n- adapters/agents/claude_code.py (modify — extract usage from result events)\n- core/state.py (modify — add usage tracking to SessionState, accumulate per-resume)\n- core/post_run.py (modify — append to usage.jsonl on notify_done)\n- host/launch.py (modify — include cost in proof-of-work comment)\n- host/cli.py (modify — add cmd_usage for querying usage.jsonl)\n- host/constants.py (modify — USAGE_LOG_FILENAME constant)\n\n1. Add `UsageData` dataclass to `core/protocols.py`: input_tokens, output_tokens, cost_usd, model\n2. In `ClaudeCodeAgent._parse()`, when `type == \"result\"`, extract `cost_usd`, `input_tokens`, `output_tokens` from the event and attach to AgentEvent\n3. In `SessionRunner`, accumulate usage from result events into `StateManager`\n4. In `StateManager`, add `update_usage()` that merges (sums tokens/cost) and persists to state.json\n5. In `post_run.notify_done()`, append a JSON line to `.nightshift/usage.jsonl` with session summary\n6. In `host/launch._post_container()`, read usage from state.json and add cost line to proof-of-work comment\n7. Add `nightshift usage` CLI command that reads and aggregates usage.jsonl\n\n- **Claude Code:** `result` event has `cost_usd`, `input_tokens`, `output_tokens` — extract directly\n- **OpenHands:** litellm does not emit usage in JSON events. May need to parse litellm debug logs or add a callback. Mark as TODO initially.\n- **Codex:** TBD — depends on event format discovery\n\n- See `core/state.py` StateManager for atomic JSON persistence\n- See `host/launch.py` _post_container() for proof-of-work comment format\n- See `host/watcher/lifecycle_comments.py` for safe comment posting\n\nREQ: new REQ-032 (token usage tracking)","files":null}]}